%`-

require KPbuild 4604

reset all

%silent = t

txt font 4
txt centre
txt c -20 "DNA Display Mode"
txt push
txt expire 12
txt font 3
txt c -40 "click on the ? button on the bottom right of this window for more information"
txt pop

txt on
txt fcolour royalblue .7
txt fill on




txt lineskip -25

txt font 4
txt fill on
txt right
txt -14 14 ? "help popup DNA.kps handoff"

alias ~knot "knot;read randorient.kps;scale 6;refine 6"
alias ~fix "fitto avlen 1;dna rand;dna twist 34"

txt font 3
txt fill on
txt select off
txt -15 60 fullscreen "full toggle"
txt -15 a  "fancy" "dna draw toggle"
txt fill off
txt -10 a toggle:

txt fill on
txt -15 a2 "pick random" "~knot;~fix"
txt push
txt phantom 4.1
txt -85 a  5.1 "load 5.1;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt -50 a0 5.2 "load 5.2;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt -15 a0 6.1 "load 6.1;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt -85 a  0.1 "load 0.1;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt -50 a0 3.1 "load 3.1;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt -15 a0 4.1 "load 4.1;scale 6;refine 6;~fix"
txt phantom
txt pop

txt fill off
txt -10 a knot:

txt fill on

txt push
txt phantom GGGGGG
txt -15 a2 CCCCCC "dna sequence C;dna twist 34"
txt -15 a GGGGGG "dna sequence G;dna twist 34"
txt -15 a TTTTTT "dna sequence T;dna twist 34"
txt -15 a AAAAAA "dna sequence A;dna twist 34"
txt -15 a random "dna rand;dna twist 34"
txt pop
txt fill off
txt -10 a resequence:


mode T

txt cent
txt fill on
txt font 3
txt c 20 "rerun demo" <DNA.kps

txt left

txt fill on
txt 15 15 cytosine "help popup cytosine.txt handoff"
txt 15 a guanine "help popup guanine.txt handoff"
txt 15 a thymine "help popup thymine.txt handoff"
txt 15 a adenine "help popup adenine.txt handoff"
txt 15 a DNA-standard "help popup DNA-standard.kps handoff"
txt fill off
txt 10 a "show definition files:"

%if macos then <DNA-fun.kps 

txt fill on
txt phantom labyrinth
txt 15 a2 labyrinth <DNA-labyrinth.kps
txt 15 a  rings <DNA-rings.kps
txt 15 a  simple <DNA-simple.kps
txt 15 a  standard <DNA-standard.kps
txt fill off
txt phantom
txt 10 a "DNA model:"

<DNA-standard.kps


txt fill off

dna scale .6
scale = .07


silent = f
~knot
~fix

exit

%`+
Help for DNA Display Mode

This is a demo of the DNA display mode for knots in KnotPlot. 
It is still under review.  Comments or suggestions are welcome.

To display a knot as DNA in KnotPlot, do the following:
   --- set display mode to DNA triads using the command
       mode T
       dna draw fancy
       dna scale .6
   --- scale your knot so that it has a average edge length of 1
       fitto avlen 1
   --- randomize the base pair sequence
       dna random
   --- fix the twisting angle (in degrees) to something realistic
       dna twist 34
   --- load the standard model definition
       <DNA-standard.kps

There are several options for the dna command in KnotPlot that
allow you to draw your basepairs pretty much arbitrarily. This
example is for the Standard Model of DNA as opposed to the 
Scharein Golden Mean and Fractal Vortex Model where each of 
the basepairs is a Fibonacci Spiral. That example will come later. 

In KP, you first say how many atoms you have and define them 
as spheres of various colours and radii:

dna atom 3               % three atom types
% usage: dna atom INDEX RADIUS RED GREEN BLUE   
dna atom 0 .75 .7 .7 .7  % carbon, a grey sphere
dna atom 1 .8  .2 .4 1   % nitrogen, a blue sphere, slightly larger than carbon
dna atom 2 .85  1 .4 .2  % oxygen, a red sphere, slightly larger than nitrogen

then you say how many base pair types you have and tell where
KnotPlot should look for the files defining the geometry of each.
In this example (following the Standard Model), there are only 4 base pairs,
but in the Scharein Golden Mean and Fractal Vortex Model there are of course
54 different base pair types.  Whatever, you can have as many as you wish. 

dna base 4                     % we have 4 base pair types
% usage: dna base INDEX DEFN_FILE
dna base 0 adenine.txt
dna base 1 thymine.txt
dna base 2 guanine.txt
dna base 3 cytosine.txt

the text files specify the layout of the atoms in that base pair.  
These consist of simple commands. The five commands are summarized below:

  s SCALE
  scale the current graphics state by the value SCALE

  t DX DY DZ
  translate the current graphics state by the vector (DX, DY, DZ)

  r ANGLE X Y Z
  rotate the current graphics state by ANGLE degrees about the axis (X, Y, Z)

  a ATOM X Y Z
  place an atom of type ATOM at location (X, Y, Z) in the current coordinate frame

  P      
  push the current graphics state onto the stack   
   
  p             
  pop the current graphics state off of the stack
